     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-family:&#39;Fira Sans&#39;,&#39;Droid Sans&#39;,arial,sans-serif;max-width:60em\"><ol style=\"margin:1.2em 0px;padding-left:2em\">\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\">Could you help me resolve this build error?</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\">I’d like to ask if you have any notes or tips for creating R packages to extend ggplot2.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">I’m trying to create my own package to extend ggplot2 for the purpose of plotting text labels that do not overlap each other.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">When trying to build <a href=\"https://github.com/jrnold/ggthemes\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/jrnold/ggthemes&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792368720259000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3ZSIl06ewU3eVUImL0R64o\">ggthemes</a> from the ZIP file downloaded from github, I encountered an error and don’t know how to resolve it. Could you help me figure this out? (I’m on OSX Yosemite)</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">I’m using RStudio and I just open the Rproj file and click “Build &amp; Reload”:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:1em;font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;,Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;overflow:auto;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:1em;font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;,Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;overflow:auto;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248);white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important;display:block;overflow-x:auto;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,248)\">==&gt; R CMD INSTALL --no-multiarch --with-keep.source ggthemes-master\r\n\r\n* installing to <span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">library</span> ‘/Library/Frameworks/R.framework/Versions/<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">3.1</span>/Resources/<span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">library</span>’\r\n* installing *<span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">source</span>* package ‘ggthemes’ <span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">...</span>\r\n** R\r\n** preparing package <span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">for</span> lazy loading\r\nWarning: package ‘ggplot2’ was built under R version <span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">3.1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">.3</span>\r\nError <span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">in</span> eval(expr, envir, enclos) : could not find <span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">function</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;ggproto&quot;</span>\r\nError : unable to load R code <span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">in</span> package ‘ggthemes’\r\nERROR: lazy loading failed <span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">for</span> package ‘ggthemes’\r\n* removing ‘/Library/Frameworks/R.framework/Versions/<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">3.1</span>/Resources/<span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">library</span>/ggthemes’\r\n\r\nExited with status <span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">1.</span>\r\n</code></pre>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">It looks like I need access to the <code style=\"font-size:1em;font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;,Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;overflow:auto;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">ggproto</code> function, but <a href=\"https://github.com/jrnold/ggthemes/search?utf8=%E2%9C%93&amp;q=ggproto\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/jrnold/ggthemes/search?utf8%3D%25E2%259C%2593%26q%3Dggproto&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792368720260000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3V2barMy6TlEDTXuZKZJF_\">it’s not referenced anywhere in the code</a>. So, I don’t know how to interpret this error.</p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:PGRpdiBzdHlsZT0iZm9udC1mYW1pbHk6IGFyaWFsLCBzYW5zLXNlcmlmOyBmb250LXNpemU6IHNt\r\nYWxsOyI+MS4gQ291bGQgeW91IGhlbHAgbWUgcmVzb2x2ZSB0aGlzIGJ1aWxkIGVycm9yPzxicj48\r\nL2Rpdj48ZGl2IHN0eWxlPSJmb250LWZhbWlseTogYXJpYWwsIHNhbnMtc2VyaWY7IGZvbnQtc2l6\r\nZTogc21hbGw7Ij4yLiBJJ2QgbGlrZSB0byBhc2sgaWYgeW91IGhhdmUgYW55IG5vdGVzIG9yIHRp\r\ncHMgZm9yIGNyZWF0aW5nIFIgcGFja2FnZXMgdG8gZXh0ZW5kIGdncGxvdDIuPC9kaXY+PGRpdiBz\r\ndHlsZT0iZm9udC1mYW1pbHk6IGFyaWFsLCBzYW5zLXNlcmlmOyBmb250LXNpemU6IHNtYWxsOyI+\r\nPGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXYgc3R5bGU9ImZvbnQtZmFtaWx5OiBhcmlhbCwgc2Fucy1zZXJpZjsgZm9u\r\ndC1zaXplOiBzbWFsbDsiPkknbSB0cnlpbmcgdG8gY3JlYXRlIG15IG93biBwYWNrYWdlIHRvIGV4\r\ndGVuZCBnZ3Bsb3QyIGZvciB0aGUgcHVycG9zZSBvZiBwbG90dGluZyB0ZXh0IGxhYmVscyB0aGF0\r\nIGRvIG5vdCBvdmVybGFwIGVhY2ggb3RoZXIuPC9kaXY+PGRpdiBzdHlsZT0iZm9udC1mYW1pbHk6\r\nIGFyaWFsLCBzYW5zLXNlcmlmOyBmb250LXNpemU6IHNtYWxsOyI+PGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXYgc3R5\r\nbGU9ImZvbnQtZmFtaWx5OiBhcmlhbCwgc2Fucy1zZXJpZjsgZm9udC1zaXplOiBzbWFsbDsiPldo\r\nZW4gdHJ5aW5nIHRvIGJ1aWxkIFtnZ3RoZW1lc10gZnJvbSB0aGUgWklQIGZpbGUgZG93bmxvYWRl\r\nZCBmcm9tIGdpdGh1YiwgSSBlbmNvdW50ZXJlZCBhbiBlcnJvciBhbmQgZG9uJ3Qga25vdyBob3cg\r\ndG8gcmVzb2x2ZSBpdC4gQ291bGQgeW91IGhlbHAgbWUgZmlndXJlIHRoaXMgb3V0PyAoSSdtIG9u\r\nIE9TWCBZb3NlbWl0ZSk8L2Rpdj48ZGl2IHN0eWxlPSJmb250LWZhbWlseTogYXJpYWwsIHNhbnMt\r\nc2VyaWY7IGZvbnQtc2l6ZTogc21hbGw7Ij48YnI+PC9kaXY+PGRpdiBzdHlsZT0iZm9udC1mYW1p\r\nbHk6IGFyaWFsLCBzYW5zLXNlcmlmOyBmb250LXNpemU6IHNtYWxsOyI+W2dndGhlbWVzXTombmJz\r\ncDtodHRwczovL2dpdGh1Yi5jb20vanJub2xkL2dndGhlbWVzPC9kaXY+PGRpdiBzdHlsZT0iZm9u\r\ndC1mYW1pbHk6IGFyaWFsLCBzYW5zLXNlcmlmOyBmb250LXNpemU6IHNtYWxsOyI+PGJyPjwvZGl2\r\nPjxkaXYgc3R5bGU9ImZvbnQtZmFtaWx5OiBhcmlhbCwgc2Fucy1zZXJpZjsgZm9udC1zaXplOiBz\r\nbWFsbDsiPkknbSB1c2luZyBSU3R1ZGlvIGFuZCBJIGp1c3Qgb3BlbiB0aGUgUnByb2ogZmlsZSBh\r\nbmQgY2xpY2sgIkJ1aWxkICZhbXA7I