     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-family:&#39;Fira Sans&#39;,&#39;Droid Sans&#39;,arial,sans-serif;max-width:60em\"><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">I have read the <a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/ggplot2/blob/master/vignettes/extending-ggplot2.Rmd\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/ggplot2/blob/master/vignettes/extending-ggplot2.Rmd&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792368720262000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0HlD0TR7XIFpsTNSTGnW30\">vignette</a> on how to extend ggplot2 and I have several questions:</p>\r\n<ol style=\"margin:1.2em 0px;padding-left:2em\">\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\">Does the vignette apply to the version of ggplot2 available from CRAN? (1.0.1)</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\">I copied and pasted the code examples into my R session and, predictably, they do not work because <code style=\"font-size:1em;font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;,Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;overflow:auto;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">ggproto</code> is not defined.</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\">Is ggplot2 meant to be extended with the simple code snippets shown in the vignette? Or, alternatively, is one supposed to create a whole new R package that imports internal ggplot2 methods?</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">I’ve created a new package with an R file like this (just a relevant snippet):</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:1em;font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;,Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;overflow:auto;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:1em;font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;,Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;overflow:auto;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248);white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important;display:block;overflow-x:auto;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,248)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">##&#39; GeomWordcloud</span>\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">##&#39; @rdname ggrepel-ggproto</span>\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">##&#39; @format NULL</span>\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">##&#39; @usage NULL</span>\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">##&#39; @importFrom ggplot2 ggproto</span>\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">##&#39; @importFrom ggplot2 GeomText</span>\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">##&#39; @importFrom grid textGrob</span>\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">##&#39; @export</span>\r\nGeomWordcloud &lt;- ggproto(<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;GeomWordcloud&quot;</span>, GeomText,\r\n</code></pre>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">As suggested in <a href=\"http://r-pkgs.had.co.nz/namespace.html#namespace-workflow\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://r-pkgs.had.co.nz/namespace.html%23namespace-workflow&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792368720262000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3ADeltMhbw_UmVVdHITQGu\">Hadley’s R package guide</a>, I run <code style=\"font-size:1em;font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;,Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;overflow:auto;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">devtools::document()</code> to generate the <code style=\"font-size:1em;font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;,Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;overflow:auto;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">NAMESPACE</code> file and receive:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:1em;font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;,Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;overflow:auto;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:1em;font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;,Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;overflow:auto;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248);white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important;display:block;overflow-x:auto;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,248)\">&gt; devtools::document()\r\nUpdating ggrepel documentation\r\nLoading ggrepel\r\nError <span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">in</span> eval(expr, envir, enclos) (from geom-wordcloud.R<span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">#89) : could not find function &quot;ggproto&quot;</span>\r\n\r\n&gt; ggplot2::ggproto\r\nError: <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&#39;ggproto&#39;</span> is not an exported object from <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&#39;namespace:ggplot2&#39;</span>\r\n</code></pre>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:PGRpdj5JIGhhdmUgcmVhZCB0aGUgW3ZpZ25ldHRlXVsxXSBvbiBob3cgdG8gZXh0ZW5kIGdncGxv\r\ndDIgYW5kIEkgaGF2ZSBzZXZlcmFsIHF1ZXN0aW9uczo8L2Rpdj48ZGl2Pjxicj48L2Rpdj48ZGl2\r\nPjEuIERvZXMgdGhlIHZpZ25ldHRlIGFwcGx5IHRvIHRoZSB2ZXJzaW9uIG9mIGdncGxvdDIgYXZh\r\naWxhYmxlIGZyb20gQ1JBTj8gKDEuMC4xKTwvZGl2PjxkaXY+Mi4gSSBjb3BpZWQgYW5kIHBhc3Rl\r\nZCB0aGUgY29kZSBleGFtcGxlcyBpbnRvIG15IFIgc2Vzc2lvbiBhbmQsIHByZWRpY3RhYmx5LCB0\r\naGV5IGRvIG5vdCB3b3JrIGJlY2F1c2UgYGdncHJvdG9gIGlzIG5vdCBkZWZpbmVkLjwvZGl2Pjxk\r\naXY+My4gSXMgZ2dwbG90MiBtZWFudCB0byBiZSBleHRlbmRlZCB3aXRoIHRoZSBzaW1wbGUgY29k\r\nZSBzbmlwcGV0cyBzaG93biBpbiB0aGUgdmlnbmV0dGU/IE9yLCBhbHRlcm5hdGl2Z