    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>On Wed, Sep 16, 2015 at 8:09 AM, Kamil Slowikowski\r<br>&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">kslowi...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt; I have read the vignette on how to extend ggplot2 and I have several\r<br>&gt; questions:\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Does the vignette apply to the version of ggplot2 available from CRAN?\r<br>&gt; (1.0.1)\r<br>&gt; I copied and pasted the code examples into my R session and, predictably,\r<br>&gt; they do not work because ggproto is not defined.\r<br>&gt; Is ggplot2 meant to be extended with the simple code snippets shown in the\r<br>&gt; vignette? Or, alternatively, is one supposed to create a whole new R package\r<br>&gt; that imports internal ggplot2 methods?\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; I’ve created a new package with an R file like this (just a relevant\r<br>&gt; snippet):\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; ##&#39; GeomWordcloud\r<br>&gt; ##&#39; @rdname ggrepel-ggproto\r<br>&gt; ##&#39; @format NULL\r<br>&gt; ##&#39; @usage NULL\r<br>&gt; ##&#39; @importFrom ggplot2 ggproto\r<br>&gt; ##&#39; @importFrom ggplot2 GeomText\r<br>&gt; ##&#39; @importFrom grid textGrob\r<br>&gt; ##&#39; @export\r<br>&gt; GeomWordcloud &lt;- ggproto(&quot;GeomWordcloud&quot;, GeomText,\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; As suggested in Hadley’s R package guide, I run devtools::document() to\r<br>&gt; generate the NAMESPACE file and receive:\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; devtools::document()\r<br>&gt; Updating ggrepel documentation\r<br>&gt; Loading ggrepel\r<br>&gt; Error in eval(expr, envir, enclos) (from geom-wordcloud.R#89) : could not\r<br>&gt; find function &quot;ggproto&quot;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; ggplot2::ggproto\r<br>&gt; Error: &#39;ggproto&#39; is not an exported object from &#39;namespace:ggplot2&#39;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>"
    ],
    [
